

Investigate the Maven Surefire test discovery issue.

The complete regression run sometimes executes
nested fixture classes as independent tests.

Important:
The Surefire -Dtest parameter overrides configured
includes and excludes.

Tasks:

1. Inspect the current Surefire configuration
   and the exact Maven command used for regression.

2. Determine whether -Dtest causes nested fixture
   classes to be selected independently.

3. Compare test discovery with and without
   the -Dtest parameter.

4. Identify the smallest reliable way to execute
   only the intended top-level test classes.

5. Ensure nested fixtures remain usable when
   launched programmatically by integration tests.

6. Do not modify production code or test logic.

7. Do not blindly add exclusion patterns to pom.xml.

8. Report the findings and recommend the smallest
   necessary change before implementing it.
